## Contract for Green

- `deliverMuseCover({ approvals, museRoot, deliveryRoot }): Promise<StorytimeManifest>` in
  `src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts`. `approvals` is the list or the path of its JSON file.
- The list is `{ version: 1, entries: [entry] }` with exactly one entry. The entry is the week entry
  without `linePrint`: `rowId` `l2-cover-v1`, `version`, optional `fileVersion`, `colorPrint`,
  optional `reviews`, optional `notes`. A `linePrint` key is refused.
- The job: id `l2-cover-v1`, size `cover`, use `cover`, directory `cover`, week 1, status `ready`, one
  candidate, no `lineArt`, file `l2-cover-v1.png`, `selectedSha256` = the color SHA-256.
- One batch `cover/color` with `batchSha256` of its file. No line-art batch.
- The color print checks of the week writer with `PICTURE_SIZES.cover`; the row id is in each error.
- The CLI: `deliver-cover --approvals <file> --muse <folder> --delivery <folder>`, paths through
  `resolveMuseDeliveryPaths`.
- Every check runs before the first write. A different `manifest.json` stops the run. A second run
  with the same inputs repeats the bytes.

